  "what_happened_next": {
    "text": "Microsoft more than tripled, while Nike lost about one-fifth of its value. Apple gained overall but suffered a fall of more than half in one month during the window. The US basket gained more steadily than that single share, though it also fell sharply at times. The ending number alone leaves out much of the experience.\n\nPathfinder reached Mars in 1997, and the euro began for financial transactions in 1999. The September 11 attacks occurred in the last month of this window, bringing devastating losses to families and communities. These are important parts of the history, rather than simple explanations for every movement in the chart.\n\nApple’s positive final return is worth comparing with its severe fall along the way. A fall of half turns $100 into $50; it then takes a doubling to get back to $100. That uneven math is one reason the route matters. An investor who needed to use the money during a low point would have had a different experience from someone able to wait.",
    "source_ids": [
      "french-us",
      "french-international",
      "fred-gs5",
      "yahoo-nke",
      "yahoo-aapl",
      "yahoo-msft",
